.TH ICLOUDCTL 1 "2026-11-14" "icloud-for-linux 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
icloudctl \- mount iCloud Drive on Linux as a local-first FUSE filesystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B icloudctl
.RI [ command ] [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B icloudctl
mounts an iCloud Drive as an ordinary folder on Linux.
.PP
The filesystem is local-first: the metadata is cached in a SQLite index, the
content is kept in a content-addressed store, and every local change is written
to a journal before it is uploaded. Reads are served from the local store and
never wait for the network.
.PP
Without a command,
.B icloudctl
prints a summary of its commands.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init \fR[\fImount_dir\fR]\fP
Create the local store, the configuration file and the systemd user unit.
The mount point defaults to \fI~/iCloud\fR.
.TP
.B configure \fR[\fIemail\fR]\fP
Write the configuration with the Apple ID. The password is read from the
terminal and stored with owner-only permissions.
.TP
.B auth \fR[\fB--force-sms\fR] [\fB--debug\fR] [\fB--accept-terms\fR]\fP
Run the interactive Apple ID sign-in and answer the two-factor challenge.
.B --force-sms
requests the code by SMS instead of waiting for the notification.
.B --debug
prints the authentication mode the service reported.
.TP
.B mount \fR[\fImount_dir\fR] [\fB--config\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB--foreground\fR]\fP
Mount the filesystem. The mount point defaults to the value in
.IR icloud.env .
Without a valid session the driver starts in unauthenticated mode and serves
the local store.
.TP
.B unmount \fR[\fImount_dir\fR]\fP
Unmount the filesystem.
.TP
.B sync \fR[\fB--dry-run\fR] [\fB--timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR]\fP
Run one synchronisation pass: drain the journal and refresh the metadata that
went stale. When the driver is running, the pass is requested over
.B SIGUSR1
and the command waits for the completion marker.
.TP
.B hydrate \fR[\fB--dry-run\fR] [\fB--path\fR \fIpath\fR]\fP
Download the content of the eligible files into the local store. With
.B --path
the subtree is listed through the service first, so a folder can be prefetched
without crawling the whole drive.
.TP
.B conflicts
List the conflicts that were preserved.
.TP
.B export-conflicts \fIdirectory\fP
Write the preserved conflict versions into a directory.
.TP
.B export \fIpath directory\fP
Materialise a subtree of the drive as plain files.
.TP
.B verify
Re-hash every blob and report corrupt blobs, missing content and working
copies that do not match the committed content.
.TP
.B gc
Remove the blobs that nothing refers to any more.
.TP
.B index
Show what the local index knows.
.TP
.B status
Show whether the service is running.
.TP
.B logs
Show the service logs.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the local setup and report what is missing.
.TP
.B clear-cache
Remove the local store. It is rebuilt on the next start.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/icloud-for-linux/config.yaml
The configuration: credentials, the store location, the synchronisation
boundary and the FUSE options.
.TP
.I ~/.config/icloud-for-linux/icloud.env
The mount point and the configuration file, as seen by the service.
.TP
.I ~/.config/icloud-for-linux/cookies
The session cookies and the session data.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/icloud-for-linux.service
The user service.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/icloud-for-linux
The local store: the content store, the working copies, the index and the
journal.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/icloud-for-linux
The logs and the completion marker of an on-demand sync.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fusermount3 (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
